<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Gestures, plus ONE narrow use of window content: putting text into the
    field the wearer is already focused on.

    This declaration used to say gesture-dispatch-only, and that the service
    "must be able to touch the screen and must not be able to read it". That
    promise was written when this was a plain mirror. It stopped being the
    honest description once the page agent existed: the agent sends a full
    picture of the screen to a vision model on every step of an errand, so
    refusing the service the ability to read a text field was withholding
    something far narrower than what the app already does in the open.

    What it buys is the one thing gestures cannot do at all. Typing by tapping
    keys is not a workaround — that is a model round trip per letter, and the
    agent's own repeat-guard blocks the second "s" in "best".

    canRetrieveWindowContent is used in exactly one place: InjectBridge.type.
    It looks for somewhere to put text — the focused node, else the nearest
    editable field beneath it, else the one in the window — and writes there.
    The search exists because input focus frequently lands on a WRAPPER rather
    than the field itself, and a wrapper refuses ACTION_SET_TEXT however
    editable its contents are; Spotify's search bar does exactly that.

    That search does visit nodes other than the focused one, so it is fair to
    call it a bounded walk rather than a single lookup. It reads only what it
    needs to answer "can this take text?" — never the text a node contains —
    it stops at 400 nodes or 12 levels, it runs ONLY during a type action, and
    it is gated behind a setting that is OFF by default.
-->
<accessibility-service xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:accessibilityEventTypes="typeViewFocused"
    android:accessibilityFeedbackType="feedbackGeneric"
    android:canPerformGestures="true"
    android:canRetrieveWindowContent="true"
    android:notificationTimeout="100"
    android:description="@string/dex_input_desc" />
